"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Select text and press **⌃⌥⌘C** to add its lines to the slot. Press again elsewhere to keep adding. The clipboard is put back, and the main window opens in front (your app stays active).\n2. Press **⌃⌥V** to paste the slot's lines one by one from the top.\n3. In the main window, pick any line and paste it.\n- Only ⌃⌥⌘C adds to the slot; a normal copy (⌘C) does not change it.\n- Pasting uses the clipboard briefly and restores it about a second later.\n\n## Main window\n- Click a line to select it (or use ↑↓) and press **Return**. The app you used last comes back and the line is pasted. A click alone does not paste.\n- **⌥Return** keeps the line in the slot; **⌘Return** adds a line break.\n- The blue number marks the line ⌃⌥V pastes next.\n- Paste All pastes every line; Clear removes the unstarred lines; Start Over restores every line added since the slot was last empty.\n\n## Stars\n- Click ☆ to make it ★. Starred lines stay in the slot after pasting. ⌃⌥V pastes them and moves on, wrapping to the top at the end.\n\n## Settings, hotkeys and permission\n- ⌃⌥⌘C adds the selection; ⌃⌥V pastes the next line. Both can be changed or turned off in Settings > Hotkey.\n- Accessibility permission is needed to send Copy and Paste to the front app.\n- To stop both hotkeys for a while, use “Pause (until relaunch)” in the menu bar menu.\n\n## Privacy\n- Everything runs on this Mac. Slot text is kept in memory only and discarded on quit.";
